I have turned into a bitter, caustic old man, where the spit of my worth hangs, from two ears, of uneven disworth, and blind to find, a swallow never kept, the taste the linging loom, to fallen court. Blow bubbles, a child hid troubles, an open mouth, and scawl a fragrant shout. Open wide, to see what is kept, a doctor or exorcism, or two woven, the eyes all, in safety slept?